# V-527 — run the canonical commit-msg hook.
#
# `core.hooksPath` is `.husky/_`, so git does NOT consult `.git/hooks/`. The
# V-205 attribution / V-211 anonymity hook was installed there by
# scripts/install-git-hooks.sh and was therefore never invoked: a message
# carrying a tool co-author trailer was accepted, while the same message run
# through the canonical hook is rejected. Husky's own `.husky/_/commit-msg`
# shim delegates to THIS file, so this is the one place the hook can be
# reached from.
#
# The banned patterns are deliberately NOT spelled out here — one list, in the
# canonical hook. Restating them would both duplicate the source of truth and
# put the very strings this hook rejects into a tracked file.
#
# Delegating rather than duplicating: scripts/git-hooks/commit-msg stays the
# single source of the patterns.
#
# Invoked through `bash` rather than executed directly, and deliberately: the
# canonical hook is not marked executable in the tree, and executing it
# directly fails with "Permission denied". Because this hook fails CLOSED that
# did not look like a broken delegation — it looked like every commit message
# being rejected, clean ones included. It also needs bash specifically; the
# pattern lists are arrays.
exec bash "$(dirname "$0")/../scripts/git-hooks/commit-msg" "$@"
